WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.569 --> 00:00:17.290
Ben gasped.

2
00:00:19.331 --> 00:00:20.873
"That mummy is your uncle?"

3
00:00:21.994 --> 00:00:22.854
Cleo nodded.

4
00:00:22.874 --> 00:00:26.858
"My uncle Tut has been missing for a thousand years.

5
00:00:27.579 --> 00:00:28.960
I never thought I'd find him here.

6
00:00:29.856 --> 00:00:31.718
The people must have kidnapped him!"

7
00:00:31.738 --> 00:00:34.420
"People are horrible!"

8
00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:35.821
said a vampire.

9
00:00:35.841 --> 00:00:39.164
"Yeah!" agreed the fish monster.

10
00:00:39.184 --> 00:00:44.828
"I think we're supposed to be giving people a chance," Ben reminded everyone.

11
00:00:44.848 --> 00:00:49.732
"Well, people aren't giving monsters a chance," said Mog.

12
00:00:49.752 --> 00:00:52.735
"They're putting mummies on display.

13
00:00:53.415 --> 00:00:55.837
This isn't a museum—it's a prison!"

14
00:00:55.857 --> 00:00:58.159
"We're all trapped!"

15
00:00:58.479 --> 00:00:59.200
added a goblin.

16
00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:01.241
Ben didn't feel trapped.

17
00:01:02.341 --> 00:01:04.683
He could float through the walls and leave at any time.

18
00:01:04.703 --> 00:01:09.025
"Cleo," he said calmly.

19
00:01:09.045 --> 00:01:13.728
"I bet there's a good explanation for why your uncle Tut is here."

20
00:01:14.688 --> 00:01:15.909
Cleo wasn't listening.

21
00:01:16.469 --> 00:01:18.930
Instead she was pounding on the display case.

22
00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:21.031
"Uncle Tut!"

23
00:01:21.932 --> 00:01:22.432
she cried.

24
00:01:22.452 --> 00:01:26.094
"Uncle Tut, can you hear me?"

25
00:01:26.114 --> 00:01:29.236
"Are you sure it's your uncle, Cleo?"

26
00:01:29.576 --> 00:01:30.436
Waldo asked.

27
00:01:30.456 --> 00:01:34.137
"You said he's been missing for a thousand years.

28
00:01:34.718 --> 00:01:36.258
How could you even recognize him?"

29
00:01:36.278 --> 00:01:40.059
"A lot of mummies look alike," Gaby chimed in.

30
00:01:40.079 --> 00:01:42.380
"I'm positive!"

31
00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:43.660
Cleo insisted.

32
00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:48.301
"My family has a statue of Uncle Tut from when he was king.

33
00:01:48.862 --> 00:01:49.802
And some paintings.

34
00:01:51.622 --> 00:01:53.463
That's definitely my uncle!"

35
00:01:54.563 --> 00:01:57.204
Just then Al Normal ran into the room.

36
00:01:58.260 --> 00:01:59.320
He looked frantic.

37
00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:01.841
"I heard a scream.

38
00:02:02.261 --> 00:02:03.642
Are you monsters okay?"

39
00:02:03.662 --> 00:02:06.402
"No." Mog shook his head.

40
00:02:06.422 --> 00:02:10.184
"Someone is killing monsters and putting them on display.

41
00:02:10.524 --> 00:02:11.284
It's not fair!"

42
00:02:12.304 --> 00:02:15.305
"What?" Al Normal shook his head in confusion.

43
00:02:15.325 --> 00:02:17.766
"No, that's not true."

44
00:02:17.786 --> 00:02:21.547
"It's not just monsters," said the fish monster.

45
00:02:21.567 --> 00:02:25.028
"I saw lots of stuffed people in the Early Humans exhibit."

46
00:02:26.436 --> 00:02:27.456
Al Normal sighed.

47
00:02:27.476 --> 00:02:30.397
"Monsters, please relax.

48
00:02:31.498 --> 00:02:33.098
Those aren't real people.

49
00:02:33.558 --> 00:02:38.139
They're dummies—life-size models made to look like cave people."

50
00:02:38.159 --> 00:02:40.440
"Oh," Mog said.

51
00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:42.541
"Well, they look pretty real."

52
00:02:42.561 --> 00:02:47.222
"Mr. Normal, are you saying that's not a real mummy?"

53
00:02:47.642 --> 00:02:49.803
Waldo asked, pointing at the display.

54
00:02:49.823 --> 00:02:53.844
"Of course it's a genuine mummy," Al Normal said.

55
00:02:54.876 --> 00:02:58.177
"All of our Egyptian displays come from ancient Egypt.

56
00:02:59.197 --> 00:03:02.678
That's the genuine mummy of Tutmosis the Thirteenth."

57
00:03:02.698 --> 00:03:04.699
"Uncle Tut!"

58
00:03:05.339 --> 00:03:06.099
Cleo wailed.

59
00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:10.140
"I told you it was my uncle Tut!

60
00:03:10.601 --> 00:03:11.801
What have you done to him?"

61
00:03:11.821 --> 00:03:16.142
"Young lady, how can he be your uncle?"

62
00:03:16.722 --> 00:03:18.423
Al Normal was growing impatient.

63
00:03:18.443 --> 00:03:20.003
"He's a mummy!"

64
00:03:20.983 --> 00:03:22.984
He blinked as he realized something.

65
00:03:26.704 --> 00:03:28.566
"Oh. You're a mummy too."

66
00:03:29.646 --> 00:03:31.207
Cleo burst into tears.

67
00:03:31.227 --> 00:03:46.156
"Wait until I tell my Al Normal patted Cleo awkwardly.

68
00:03:46.276 --> 00:03:48.898
"There's no reason to cry.

69
00:03:48.918 --> 00:03:52.360
I promise, we didn't do anything to your uncle.

70
00:03:53.676 --> 00:03:58.239
Tutmosis was that way when he came here—way before I was born."

71
00:03:58.259 --> 00:04:02.301
"Maybe he's just asleep," Ben said.

72
00:04:02.321 --> 00:04:05.042
"I think I see him breathing."

73
00:04:05.062 --> 00:04:08.184
"You're right!"

74
00:04:08.664 --> 00:04:10.646
Cleo started pounding on the case again.

75
00:04:10.666 --> 00:04:12.166
"Uncle Tut!

76
00:04:12.547 --> 00:04:14.147
Uncle Tut, wake up!"

77
00:04:15.508 --> 00:04:17.910
Other monsters started banging on the case too.

78
00:04:17.930 --> 00:04:19.430
"Uncle Tut!

79
00:04:19.771 --> 00:04:20.751
Wake up!"

80
00:04:24.892 --> 00:04:27.093
"Monsters!" Miss Bungle called.

81
00:04:27.113 --> 00:04:28.674
"Please settle down.

82
00:04:29.034 --> 00:04:30.755
You're behaving like people!"

83
00:04:31.395 --> 00:04:32.735
Just then Mr.

84
00:04:32.795 --> 00:04:34.836
Freaky came running into the exhibit room.

85
00:04:35.597 --> 00:04:37.558
Dr. Bones was right behind him.

86
00:04:37.578 --> 00:04:40.479
"Monsters, please!"

87
00:04:40.859 --> 00:04:41.959
Mr. Freaky cried.

88
00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:45.281
He took out his handkerchief and blew his noses.

89
00:04:51.063 --> 00:04:52.324
is going on in here?"

90
00:04:53.372 --> 00:04:55.313
Dr. Bones rushed toward Cleo.

91
00:04:56.514 --> 00:04:58.074
"Stop that at once!"

92
00:04:58.615 --> 00:04:59.175
she ordered.

93
00:05:00.015 --> 00:05:03.477
She tried to pull Cleo and the other monsters away from the case.

94
00:05:04.457 --> 00:05:08.619
But everyone kept shouting and banging.

95
00:05:08.639 --> 00:05:13.541
"Ben's right," Waldo said.

96
00:05:13.561 --> 00:05:16.442
"Uncle Tut is definitely breathing.

97
00:05:17.403 --> 00:05:19.524
If he wakes up, Cleo, he can go home with you."

98
00:05:20.168 --> 00:05:21.108
Cleo looked at him.

99
00:05:21.129 --> 00:05:23.149
"That would be so great.

100
00:05:23.490 --> 00:05:24.910
But how can we wake him up?"

101
00:05:24.930 --> 00:05:29.092
"I could throw the case in the fountain," Gaby suggested.

102
00:05:29.112 --> 00:05:31.093
"The cold water might wake him up."

103
00:05:32.573 --> 00:05:34.774
"Uh Ben glanced uneasily at Dr.

104
00:05:34.794 --> 00:05:39.977
Bones. "I don't think the people would like that," he said.

105
00:05:39.997 --> 00:05:44.839
"Maybe I could float through the case and shake him awake."

106
00:05:44.859 --> 00:05:47.540
"Good idea," Winnie said.

107
00:05:48.468 --> 00:05:53.111
"My spell book is upstairs with my stuff," Waldo said, reaching into his pockets.

108
00:05:53.131 --> 00:05:55.012
"But I have a wand with me.

109
00:05:55.332 --> 00:05:56.532
I can try a magic spell."

110
00:05:58.053 --> 00:06:01.115
"Oh no," Ben thought, trying not to groan.

111
00:06:01.915 --> 00:06:02.816
By now Dr.

112
00:06:02.856 --> 00:06:03.836
Bones was shouting.

113
00:06:03.856 --> 00:06:05.677
"Monster children!

114
00:06:05.978 --> 00:06:08.999
Step away from the displays right now!"

115
00:06:09.019 --> 00:06:11.260
"It's not a display!"

116
00:06:11.641 --> 00:06:12.361
Cleo wailed.

117
00:06:12.381 --> 00:06:13.862
"It's my uncle!"

118
00:06:14.542 --> 00:06:15.883
Waldo pointed his wand.

119
00:06:15.903 --> 00:06:17.504
"Wake up!"

120
00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:18.640
he cried.

121
00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:22.141
Ka-zap! Bing!

122
00:06:22.621 --> 00:06:24.662
The spell bounced off the glass case.

123
00:06:25.342 --> 00:06:28.023
Monsters covered their heads and dived out of the way.

124
00:06:28.403 --> 00:06:31.424
The spell zapped over their heads and shot into the next room.

125
00:06:32.184 --> 00:06:34.264
Cleo peeled her hand away from her eyes.

126
00:06:34.284 --> 00:06:36.265
"Did the spell work?"

127
00:06:36.685 --> 00:06:38.005
she asked in a hushed voice.

128
00:06:39.286 --> 00:06:41.386
Ben turned to look at the display case.

129
00:06:42.066 --> 00:06:44.887
Unfortunately Uncle Tut was still inside.

130
00:06:45.888 --> 00:06:47.328
Then he heard Winnie gasp.

131
00:06:48.024 --> 00:06:50.286
"It worked on something!"

132
00:06:50.907 --> 00:06:53.169
she said, pointing to the next room.

133
00:06:53.189 --> 00:06:56.672
"The museum's dinosaur skeletons have come to life!"
